Fcitx5 for Android Contributors: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

pis additions and modifications include the keyboard layout and minimal settings,
candidate/translation presentation, native translation integration, offline voice
coordination, user-frequency controls and input/feedback changes.
See CHANGES.md, LICENSING.md, LICENSE and LICENSES/.

Native components include Fcitx5, Chinese addons, libime, KenLM, Yoga, Fcitx5 Lua,
Boost, libintl-lite, libuv, Lua, zstd, OpenCC and marisa-trie. Individual source
files and component notices specify the applicable licenses.

Translation uses llama.cpp (MIT) and Tencent Hy-MT2-1.8B-GGUF (Apache-2.0).
Speech uses sherpa-onnx 1.13.8 (Apache-2.0) and ONNX Runtime 1.28.2 (MIT and
third-party notices). The official AAR also contains eSpeak NG (GPLv3),
Piper Phonemize (MIT) and other native dependencies. Their license notices and
corresponding source/build information are provided with the release materials.

Speech and punctuation model sources and licenses are recorded in
docs/compliance/MODELS.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Original license texts, copyright notices, source attribution and modifications
are retained in the repository and release materials.
